      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has major understandability issues:\n1. All `data_samples()` rows are crammed onto a few lines — unreadable\n2. Many unused data provider methods bloat the file (only `data_samples` is referenced)\n3. Many unused imports\n\nI'll write a clean version that keeps the same test logic, formats `data_samples()` readably, and removes the dead code.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused data provider methods and unused imports, and reformats `data_samples()` with one entry per line grouped by scenario (early Julian dates, leap years, century years, BC dates, 1582 cutover, British cutover transition, lenient gap dates, and modern Gregorian dates), making the test's intent immediately clear."
    }
